  </revision>
  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>af34ed8981922b2a153a3a50bed91bb5</srcmd5>
    <version>1.66.1</version>
    <time>1788963607</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to containerized-data-importer 1.66.1 and security re-vendor of the bundled Go dependencies (tarball rebuilt from v1.66.1 with updated go.mod/vendor; upstream sources unchanged).

1.66.1 upstream changes:
- import into 4k-sector block devices no longer fails (qemu fix pulled into the importer image build)
- nbdkit nfc support for vSphere disk imports
- minimum PVC size for the HPE XP and Hitachi HSPC provisioners

v1.66.1 ships the same pristine vendor tree as v1.66.0, so this carries the 1.66.0 bumps forward (golang.org/x/net 0.57.0, moby/spdystream 0.5.1, ulikunitz/xz 0.5.15, go-jose/go-jose/v3 3.0.5) and adds:
- google.golang.org/grpc 1.79.3 -&gt; 1.83.1: CVE-2026-84304 (bsc#1279234), CVE-2026-84303 (bsc#1279315)
- golang.org/x/crypto 0.54.0 -&gt; 0.56.0: CVE-2026-56854, CVE-2026-56855, CVE-2026-78662 (bsc#1278621)
- go.opentelemetry.io/otel 1.39.0 -&gt; 1.44.0: CVE-2026-41178 (bsc#1276687)
- golang.org/x/text 0.40.0 -&gt; 0.41.0 (required by x/crypto 0.56.0)

golang.org/x/crypto 0.56.0 requires Go 1.26, so BuildRequires moves to golang(API) &gt;= 1.26. _service revision follows the tag.
</comment>
